I. COMPILATION

The compilation of this version works with modern gfortran and intel compilers.
To complie, follow the instructions:

	cd clustering_program/
	make clean
	make



II. FILES GENERATED BY MAKEFILE:

All binary files are located in the same folder. The programs to execute are:
	
	1. make_matrix: generates a distance matrix based on a specified criterion:

    		-rmsd: computes the root-mean-square deviation (RMSD) differences among encounter complexes.
    		-z_coord: calculates the difference in distance to z = 0 for specified atoms among encounter complexes.
    		-atoms_dist: computes the difference in distances between specified atoms among encounter complexes.
    		-angle: evaluates the difference in angles between two vectors formed by given groups of atoms.

	2. clust: performs cluster analysis using a previously generated distance matrix.

	3. analyze_residues: identifies residues that are within a specified threshold distance from the z-plane.



III. EXAMPLES:

1. Clustering based on the copper atom distance of solute 2 to the z-plane

./make_matrix -pdb2 p2_noh.pdb -atoms2 Cu -complexes assoc_complexes -matrix_type z_coord -matrix matrix_z.txt -array array_z.txt -nb_encounters 10000

./clust -complexes assoc_complexes -matrix matrix_z.txt -array array_z.txt -nb_encounters 10000 -k_factor 1.0 -output_name Cu_z


2. Clustering based on the the copper atom distance of solute 2 to the C1 atoms of solute 1

./make_matrix -pdb1 p1_noh.pdb -pdb2 p2_noh.pdb -atoms1 C1 -atoms2 Cu -complexes Cu_z_cluster0001_complexes -matrix_type atoms_dist -matrix matrix_C1_dist.txt -array array_C1_dist.txt -nb_encounters 10000

./clust -complexes Cu_z_cluster0001_complexes -matrix matrix_C1_dist.txt -array array_C1_dist.txt -nb_encounters 10000 -k_factor 1.0 -output_name C1_dist


3. Clustering based on the angle formed between the surface chain of solute 1 and the copper-histidine vector of solute 2

./make_matrix -pdb1 p1_noh.pdb -pdb2 p2_noh.pdb -atoms1 1 -atoms2 411 -atoms3 Cu -atoms4 4 5 6 7 8 -complexes Cu_z_cluster0001_complexes -matrix_type atoms_dist -matrix matrix_C1_dist.txt -array array_C1_dist.txt -nb_encounters 10000

NOTE: -atoms1 and -atoms2 are the group of atoms of solute 1 to form vector 1. -atoms3 and -atoms4 are the group of atoms of sollute 2 to form vector 2

./clust -complexes Cu_z_cluster0001_complexes -matrix matrix_C1_dist.txt -array array_C1_dist.txt -nb_encounters 10000 -k_factor 1.0 -output_name C1_dist
